20260527.113005.096 [<ideas.........] [The user seeks three distinct explanations for why pytest encounters an ImportError related to an undefined symbol]
20260527.113007.422 [<ideas.........] [cblas_dgemm when trying to load enn_rust.so within a conda environment that uses separate libblas and libcblas libraries.]
20260527.113007.575 [<ideas.........] [The ImportError occurs because enn_rust.so links against BLAS libraries but fails to resolve the CBLAS symbol cblas_dgemm at]
20260527.113007.712 [<ideas.........] [import time. This happens due to conda's separation of libblas and libcblas libraries, where CBLAS functions like]
20260527.113007.863 [<ideas.........] [cblas_dgemm reside in a distinct shared object. Since the build links against a BLAS implementation with rpath, but CBLAS is]
20260527.113008.029 [<ideas.........] [in a different library, the dynamic linker cannot resolve cblas_dgemm during pytest's import phase. The issue arises]
20260527.113008.118 [<ideas.........] [specifically because the CBLAS API differs from vanilla BLAS, and the shared library chain doesn't properly link these]
20260527.113009.017 [<ideas.........] [symbols together.]
