20260527.113037.927 [<ideas.........] [I now have a clear understanding of the formal system.]
20260527.113038.113 [<ideas.........] [The Rust extension `enn_rust.so` is built as a cdylib using maturin and repaired with auditwheel on Linux, dynamically]
20260527.113038.341 [<ideas.........] [linking to BLAS/OpenBLAS through build scripts that detect `libblas.so` or `libopenblas.so` but not `libcblas.so`. Faiss's]
20260527.113038.536 [<ideas.........] [linking chain expects C BLAS symbols, which causes issues when `libcblas.so` is not explicitly linked. Conda-forge splits]
20260527.113038.712 [<ideas.........] [BLAS into separate packages: `libblas` (Fortran BLAS) and `libcblas` (C BLAS wrapper), leading to symbol resolution problems]
20260527.113038.915 [<ideas.........] [where `cblas_dgemm` is undefined because it's not exported from the loaded shared object. Additionally, pytest loads `enn`]
20260527.113039.638 [<ideas.........] [early during import, triggering dynamic loading before NumPy, SciPy, or PyTorch can establish proper `LD_PRELOAD` ordering.]
20260527.113039.812 [<ideas.........] [The issue isn't that BLAS is missing, but rather that too many BLAS implementations are partially satisfied, causing symbol]
20260527.113040.020 [<ideas.........] [resolution conflicts. Asymptotically, each pytest worker and optional import adds more DT_NEEDED edges, and at N concurrent]
20260527.113040.351 [<ideas.........] [collectors, the dynamic linker resolves an inconsistent union of symbolswhere `cblas_dgemm` is satisfied from one library]
20260527.113042.379 [<ideas.........] [while `dgemm` comes from another, worsening with pytest testmon spawning.]
20260527.113042.591 [<ideas.........] [The import graph is so extensive that the "first resolver wins" policy never encounters `libcblas` even though it exists on]
20260527.113042.608 [<ideas.........] [disk.  ]
20260527.113043.075 [<ideas.........] [The bug stems from a mismatch between link-editor and loader semantics regarding split SONAME, not rpathon CI manylinux,]
20260527.113043.093 [<ideas.........] [`UNDEF cblas_dgemm` was linked against `libcblas.so`, but in the conda environment, `libcblas` was replaced with a]
20260527.113044.231 [<ideas.........] [compatibility symlink farm where `libblas.so` re-exports nothing and `libcblas` is loaded lazily.]
20260527.113044.461 [<ideas.........] [Pathological edge: `libblas.so` exists, so `blas_libs_present` returns true and adds rpath to `$CONDA_PREFIX/lib`, masking]
20260527.113044.633 [<ideas.........] [the missing `libcblas` from the detection predicate  the build "succeeds" but creates a runtime trap.]
20260527.113044.785 [<ideas.........] [Asymptotic scaling: pytest is the probe, not the victim  pytests import order is the sole activity that triggers the]
20260527.113046.391 [<ideas.........] [lazy-binding edge, making it the key factor in exposing the issue.]
20260527.113046.533 [<ideas.........] [The `enn_rust.so` module loads successfully in direct Python execution but fails under pytest due to testmon or conftest]
20260527.113046.729 [<ideas.........] [loading a stub module that dlopen's a stripped auditwheel copy, whereas editable installs point to a different binary with]
20260527.113046.941 [<ideas.........] [differing NEEDED entries. A pathological scenario arises when two versions of `enn_rust.so` exist on PYTHONPATHpytest]
20260527.113047.161 [<ideas.........] [selects the wheel copy lacking `libcblas` dependencies, while the editable version shadows it. Furthermore, auditwheels]
20260527.113047.195 [<ideas.........] [assumption leads to complications where libopenblas is copied into wheels, yet in conda environments, these blobs export]
20260527.113049.131 [<ideas.........] [only Fortran BLAS symbols, leaving CBLAS symbols unresolved.]
20260527.113049.380 [<ideas.........] [Wheel repair incorrectly removed the DT_NEEDED entry for libcblas, assuming that openblas provides it.  ]
20260527.113049.685 [<ideas.........] [The symbol `cblas_dgemm` originates from cblas-sys within the Rust ndarray stack, not from Faiss.  ]
20260527.113049.730 [<ideas.........] [The build scripts for enn-py and ennbo differ in their linking behavioronly ennbo links cblas, while enn-py does not,]
20260527.113051.613 [<ideas.........] [despite both being part of the same project.]
20260527.113051.783 [<ideas.........] **Formal system (shared rules):** `enn_rust.so` is a Linux cdylib built via maturin; BLAS/CBLAS is satisfied through dynamic
20260527.113052.476 [<ideas.........] linking and build-time probes (`blas_libs_present`, `has_blas_for_link`, OpenBLAS path injection); conda often ships
20260527.113052.795 [<ideas.........] **split** `libblas` / `libcblas`; pytest fails at **import** with `undefined symbol: cblas_dgemm`, not during a numerical
20260527.113052.827 [<ideas.........] test assertion.
20260527.113053.438 [<ideas.........] Core assumptions being stressed: (1) one coherent BLAS provider at load time, (2) seeing `libblas.so` means CBLAS is
20260527.113054.139 [<ideas.........] covered, (3) the failing `.so` is the one you just built, (4) import order is irrelevant once `rpath` is set, (5) the
20260527.113054.553 [<ideas.........] missing symbol’s origin matches whichever crate linked BLAS.
20260527.113054.581 [<ideas.........] ---
20260527.113055.091 [<ideas.........] ### Idea 1 — Split-BLAS “presence trap” (negation of “if BLAS is there, linking is correct”)
20260527.113055.466 [<ideas.........] **Assumption pushed:** `blas_libs_present` / `has_blas_for_link` treat existence of `libblas.so` or `libopenblas.so` as
20260527.113055.780 [<ideas.........] proof that the **entire** BLAS+CBLAS surface is available from that directory.
20260527.113056.489 [<ideas.........] **Extreme / pathological case:** Conda’s layout is intentionally **factored**: Fortran BLAS in `libblas.so`, CBLAS entry
20260527.113057.431 [<ideas.........] points (`cblas_dgemm`) only in `libcblas.so`, with no re-export bridge. Build emits `-Wl,-rpath,$CONDA_PREFIX/lib` because
20260527.113058.023 [<ideas.........] `libblas.so` exists, so the linker records a successful link against a BLAS **family** while leaving `cblas_dgemm` as a
